[
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev22-01",
    "question": "<p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_{1}\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{i}+2\\mathbf{k}+\\lambda(2\\mathbf{i}+3\\mathbf{j}-\\mathbf{k})\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda\"></span> is a scalar parameter.</p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_{2}\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{x+1}{1}=\\frac{y-4}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{3}\"></span></p><p>(a) Prove that the lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_{1}\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_{2}\"></span> are skew. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(b) Find the shortest distance between the lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_{1}\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_{2}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p>The plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi\"></span> contains <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_{1}\"></span> and intersects <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_{2}\"></span> at the point (3, 8, 13).</p><p>(c) Find a cartesian equation for the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi.\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>Nonparallel lines can still fail to intersect in three dimensions. Test all three component equations using the same pair of parameters. Their shortest separation is the component of a joining vector in the direction perpendicular to both lines, obtained using the cross product of their directions.</p>",
      "<p>(a) Parametrise <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,4,1)+\\mu(1,1,3)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>The directions <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,3,-1)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,1,3)\"></span> are not proportional. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Equating <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x,y\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=6,\\mu=14\"></span>, but the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span> coordinates are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4,43\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Thus the lines neither intersect nor are parallel, so they are skew. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) A common normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,3,-1)\\times(1,1,3)=(10,-7,-1)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>The displacement between the given base points is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,4,-1)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Its scalar projection onto the normal has magnitude <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|-20-28+1|/\\sqrt{150}=47/\\sqrt{150}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(c) Join <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,0,2)\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,8,13)\"></span> to get a second in-plane vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,8,11)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Crossing this with the line direction gives a normal <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(41,-24,10)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Substitution of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,0,2)\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"41x-24y+10z=61\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 13 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev22-01-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2018 FP3 · Q6, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev22-01-ms-02.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2018 FP3 · Q6, extract 2\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev22-01-ms-03.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2018 FP3 · Q6, extract 3\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev22-01-ms-04.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2018 FP3 · Q6, extract 4\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>",
