  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev22-02",
    "question": "<p>The plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{1}\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x-2 y-3 z=5\"></span> and the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{2}\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6 x+y-4 z=7\"></span></p><p>(a) Find, to the nearest degree, the acute angle between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{1}\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{2}\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>The point P has coordinates (2,3,-1). The line l is perpendicular to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{1}\"></span> and passes through the point P. The line l intersects <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{2}\"></span> at the point Q.</p><p>(b) Find the coordinates of Q.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>The plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{3}\"></span> passes through the point Q and is perpendicular to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{1}\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{2}\"></span></p><p>(c) Find an equation of the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{3}\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{r}.\\mathbf{n}=p\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>Each plane&#x27;s normal can be read from its Cartesian coefficients. The acute angle between the planes is the acute angle between the normals. To project a point, travel along the normal of the target plane until the moving coordinates satisfy its equation.</p>",
      "<p>(a) Use the normals <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf n_1=(1,-2,-3),\\ \\mathbf n_2=(6,1,-4)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Their dot product is 16, so the acute angle is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\arccos[16/\\sqrt{14\\cdot53}]\\approx54^\\circ\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) The perpendicular line has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=(2,3,-1)+t(1,-2,-3)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Substitution into the second plane gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"19+16t=7\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=-3/4\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q=(5/4,9/2,5/4)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(c) The required normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf n_1\\times\\mathbf n_2=(11,-14,13)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> its scalar product is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-33\"></span>, so the plane is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r\\cdot(11,-14,13)=-33\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 11 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev22-02-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2017 FP3 · Q5, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev22-02-ms-02.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2017 FP3 · Q5, extract 2\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev22-03",
    "question": "<p>The plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{1}\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"x-5 y-2 z=3\"></div><p>The plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{2}\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{i}+2\\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k}+\\lambda(\\mathbf{i}+4\\mathbf{j}+3\\mathbf{k})+\\mu(2\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}+\\mathbf{k})\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu\"></span> are scalar parameters.</p><p>(a) Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{1}\"></span> is perpendicular to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{2}\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(b) Find a cartesian equation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{2}\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(c) Find an equation for the line of intersection of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{1}\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\varPi_{2}\"></span> giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\mathbf{r}-\\mathbf{a}) \\times\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{0}\"></span> , where a and b are constant vectors to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>Take the cross product of the two in-plane directions to obtain a normal. Its scalar product with the other plane&#x27;s normal tests perpendicularity. For the intersection line, its direction must instead be perpendicular to both normals, so take their cross product.</p>",
      "<p>(a) A normal to the second plane is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,4,3)\\times(2,-1,1)=(7,5,-9)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Its scalar product with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,-5,-2)\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7-25+18=0\"></span>, so the planes are perpendicular. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) Substituting the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,2,1)\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7x+5y-9z=8\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(c) A line direction is proportional to the cross product of the normals, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(55,-5,40)\"></span>, so take <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf b=(11,-1,8)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>To find a point, set <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=-1\"></span>. Then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x-5y=1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"7x+5y=-1\"></span>, giving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0,y=-1/5\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\mathbf r-(0,-1/5,-1))\\times(11,-1,8)=\\mathbf0\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 12 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev22-03-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2016 FP3 · Q8, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev22-03-ms-02.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2016 FP3 · Q8, extract 2\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev22-03-ms-03.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2016 FP3 · Q8, extract 3\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev22-03-ms-04.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2016 FP3 · Q8, extract 4\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev22-03-ms-05.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for June 2016 FP3 · Q8, extract 5\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
